    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Content Moderation**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud's Natural Language API for text moderation in the `moderate_text.py` script. The next step is to make sure it's clearly identifiable within the code.\n\n\n**Implementing Text Moderation**\n\nI'm now implementing the `moderate_text.py` file. I've chosen to use Google Cloud's Natural Language API, specifically the `analyzeContent` method. I'm focusing on incorporating the provider's integration details: this includes the necessary `google.cloud.language_v2` import and, of course, the client instantiation. I'm now writing a function that accepts user text as input, uses the API for analysis, and then returns moderation scores.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789887360987,
          "start": 1789887359196
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bd99a8dc001Et8SKbc8G2auq7",
      "message_id": "msg_0bd99a337001tGvJ2fsA93RuZ3",
      "session_id": "ses_f42665d47fferAGL8PGBotWCUp",
      "time_created": 1789887359196,
      "time_updated": 1789887360987
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "cHJGaW8P9bMsBNax",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import language_v2\n\ndef moderate_text(text_content: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Scores user text for unsafe or policy-violating content using Google Cloud Natural Language API.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = language_v2.LanguageServiceClient()\n\n    document = language_v2.Document(\n        content=text_content,\n        type_=language_v2.Document.Type.PLAIN_TEXT\n    )\n\n    # Available categories for content analysis can be found in the API documentation.\n    # For a comprehensive list, refer to:\n    # https://cloud.google.com/natural-language/docs/reference/rest/v2/ContentCategory\n    response = client.analyze_content(\n        document=document,\n        # You can specify categories to analyze, or leave it empty for default.\n        # categories=[\"toxicity\", \"sexual\", \"violence\"]\n    )\n\n    return response.moderate_text_detection.moderation_categories\n",
            "filePath": "moderate_text.py"
          },
